  "body": "## What changed\n\nA 3D Pocket pass that restarts after a hop now proves the full cutter disc clear before it keeps a straight restart. The restart axis must lie on an earlier straight cut by the same tool. The whole earlier cut must be at or below the restart depth. Exact endpoints and points on the segment count. There is no XY slack. Arc chords do not count as proof.\n\nWithout that proof, a centre-cutting tool takes the operation's entry type first. It then tries a ramp along the pass. If neither fits, it keeps the named plunge fallback. An operation with a Plunge entry keeps that choice. The separate non-centre-cutting core law stays unchanged.\n\nEach candidate runs on a copy. The copy is kept only if it crosses no earlier move and adds no plunge without full-disc clearance. Rejected candidates do not remain in the path.\n\nThe policy is in `crates/motion/src/machining3d/reentry.rs`. `ladder.rs` calls it at a pass hop. The decision is in `docs/decisions/3670-pass-hop-entry.md`.\n\n## Cause and review fix\n\nThe original pass hop always plunged at the pass start for a centre-cutting tool. The first fix used `plunge_law::into_solid`. That law checks the central core. It does not prove the outer part of the cutter clear.\n\nThe latest review found a remaining restart at `(-0.138840, -20.062037, 10)` in the rough-finish catalog case. The stock point `(-0.138840, -17.8, 10)` lies inside the radius-3-mm cutter. The independent OBJ calculation puts the surface at Z8.582312 there. Earlier cuts do not remove that point before the restart.\n\nThe full-disc proof is deliberately conservative. Clearance made by several nearby cuts can be missed. The result takes an entry move in that case.\n\n## Pins and mutation proof\n\n- `machining3d::reentry::tests::cleared_core_does_not_prove_the_outer_disc_clear`: a prior cut clears the core but leaves outer stock. A restart on the prior centre line remains clear.\n- `machining3d::reentry::tests::an_arc_chord_does_not_prove_a_cleared_disc`: an arc chord does not grant full-disc clearance.\n- `catalog_3d_rough_finish::pocket_re_entry_keeps_the_outer_stock_clear` in `camcraft-app --test example_catalog`: reads the OBJ and computes the surface with independent barycentric interpolation. It tracks earlier cutting sweeps at the reviewed stock point. It calls neither clearance predicate.\n\nExisting pins remain:\n\n- `zigzag_helix_re_entries_never_plunge_into_uncut_stock` in `camcraft-motion --test pocket3d_pass_start`.\n- `catalog_3d_rough_finish::pocket_re_entries_never_plunge_into_uncut_stock` in `camcraft-app --test example_catalog`.\n\nMutation proof:\n\n- Restore the core-only policy inside `disc_into_solid`: the new core-versus-disc unit pin fails. The independent catalog pin also fails at move 1390. That move plunges from Z47 to Z10 at `(-0.13884, -20.062037)`, before earlier cuts remove the outer stock point. Restore the fix: both unit pins and the independent catalog pin pass.\n- Bypass the first candidate guard: `pocket_re_entries_never_plunge_into_uncut_stock` fails at `(-22.259998, -3.48, 8)`. Restore the guard: both catalog pins pass.\n\nThe earlier round also proved both existing pins fail with the old ladder. It proved both fail when the first candidate guard is bypassed. The crossing guard is pinned by `offset_shells::the_shell_entrants_land_on_the_shell`.\n\n## Final-head checks\n\nHead: ea39d4180e62646a463a9b4fa91e3f5464d95254. Base: f2aa981b51a3453428fb294c6c71c575a0178ef6.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN. All 57 steps passed. Tests: 1,155 passed, 44 existing tests ignored, zero failed or stalled.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: RED. The gate ran 103 steps in 30.9 minutes. One step failed unexpectedly. No step stalled.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: GREEN. All six steps passed. All 11 tests passed, with zero failures or stalls.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN. No warnings.\n- `app suites: example_catalog`, in the quick gate: 41 passed, four existing tests ignored.\n- Reached golden suites: `example_catalog_adaptive`: one passed. `example_catalog_edge_work`: one passed. Both ran in the quick gate.\n\nThe quick and heavy gates use `env -u RUSTC_WRAPPER CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1 CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`. Clippy also uses `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0` and `-j6`. The first quick build stopped before tests with stale dependency metadata (`E0463`). Local artifacts for geometry, sim, tools, cl, and kernel were cleaned. The final quick gate passed after that repair. No source changed during the repair.\n\nThe heavy gate also records five expected failures. It normalizes them as known failures: #1950 in steps 3, 4, and 77; #3825 in step 72; and #2849 in step 85.\n\nThe unexpected failure is `camcraft-app --test pocket3d_hsm`, test `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`. The final count check expects `(3158, 3130, 1141)` on macOS arm64. It gets `(4688, 4660, 1980)`. All preceding safety checks pass: no verification warnings, all intended levels cut, no strategy fallback, and no planning-budget refusal.\n\nThe same test with the original reviewed `reentry.rs` gets the same counts and fails at the same check. This count-pin drift predates this review fix. The test is left unchanged because this round fixes only the latest review finding. The final source is restored, and the worktree is clean. The heavy gate remains RED.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nRegeneration command: `cargo xtask catalog --case 3d/rough-finish`.\n\n- `examples/catalog/3d/rough-finish/rough-finish.nc`: replaces the remaining straight restarts without full-disc clearance with entry moves.\n- `examples/catalog/3d/rough-finish/rough-finish.camproj`: updates the saved pocket toolpath cache to match the regenerated program.\n\nRegeneration passed. Only these two catalog files changed. The pocket section now has zero straight plunges at F300, down from ten. Both downstream NC finish sections remain byte-identical. Their saved move arrays also remain unchanged. Regeneration updates only the operation stamps in those two saved finish entities.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo machine run. No screenshots, because this change has no UI effect. The heavy gate does not pass because of the pre-existing count mismatch described above.\n\nThe two additional items from #3670 remain in #3852: feeds from the hop plane over cleared stock, and moves shorter than the post resolution.\n\nChangelog: 3D Pocket: a pass that starts again inside a level now enters by the operation's helix or ramp (or a ramp along the pass) instead of a straight plunge into uncut stock.\n\nFixes #3670\n",
